WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.510
<i>Suguru Aizawa and Kakeru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.690
<i>The dream of these 
soccer-loving brothers</i>

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:11.120
<i>was to play in the World 
Cup together and win.</i>

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>The older brother continued to improve</i>

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.390
<i>and took on the world 
wearing the blue 10 jersey.</i>

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.490
<i>He came to be known as the 
"treasure of Japanese soccer."</i>

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.650
<i>His brother, who frantically 
tried to catch up,</i>

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.420
<i>had almost realized their dreams.</i>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.730
<i>Or so it should have been.</i>

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.550
<i>By an unfortunate accident,</i>

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.380
<i>the Aizawa brothers 
arrived at death's door.</i>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.050
<i>Despite desperate treatment,</i>

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.970
<i>the older brother would not return.</i>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.370
<i>The younger, Kakeru,</i>

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.000
<i>having sustained great 
injury to his heart,</i>

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.820
<i>straddled the boundary 
between life and death.</i>

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.580
<i>There was only one path to 
survival: a heart transplant.</i>

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.150
I kept believing it. 
My dream. 
Our dream!

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.520
<i>Kakeru received his brother's heart</i>

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.620
<i>and his proud will.</i>

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.570
<i>To realize their dream,
 Kakeru ran forward once again.</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.280
<i>His life as a soccer player 
was only just beginning.</i>

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.530
<i>The Kanagawa High School 
Championship quarterfinals.</i>

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:38.440
<i>We're up against Sagamigaura, 
who defeated Shonan.</i>

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.470
<i>The night before the match,</i>

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.900
<i>thanks to Hibino-kun and his team,</i>

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.020
<i>we were able to experience the</i>

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.630
<i>new Total Foot for the first time.</i>

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.860
<i>Then, finally, the kickoff.</i>

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.600
<i>We thought we were ready for it,</i>

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.480
<i>but the real thing was amazing.</i>

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.860
<i>The match is only getting started.</i>

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.520
<i>Everyone, do your best!</i>

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:58.030
New Total Football.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:02.090
Show them the strategy that will 
change high school soccer.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:08.950
<b>Storm Warning!</b>

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.870
<b><i>Enoshima</i></b>

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.870
<b><i>Sagamigaura</i></b>

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.340
It's about time you gave up that ball.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.590
We're only just getting started.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.250
Sagamigaura, who have been

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.000
sending around only short passes,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.310
suddenly sends out a long 
pass for a side change.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.520
I won't let you keep it!

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:38.900
Of course I won't.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.740
<i>It's as if these guys know 
where the ball is going to be.</i>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.170
The essence of offense in soccer

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.830
is in the exchange between 
slow and fast, long and short.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.130
From a short pass to a long.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.390
From to-and-fro short movements

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.670
to a sudden attack on the area.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.060
The defenders, who've gotten 
used to one or the other,

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.930
won't be able to change over quickly.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.230
Horikawa, take care 
of the opposite side.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.350
Got it.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.140
<i>Why are so many players attacking?</i>

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.060
Here!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.380
All right!

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:21.320
Kazuhide's centering puts the 
ball in front of the goal!

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.030
Cra—

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.910
He's on the other side 
of the goalkeeper, Ri.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.080
Tsuguhide is lining up 
the cross. Watch out!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.790
It's mine!

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.250
It's Aizawa!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.340
What? How did he...

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.300
Kakeru!

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.340
I won't let you shoot!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.800
Yeah, right.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.810
He shoots!

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.650
The ball is sucked towards 
the opposite corner

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.870
from the goal keeper, Ri.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.260
He stops it!

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.260
He pushes it away with a sideways jump.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.540
The defensive player, Ri's, super save

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.610
takes Enoshima out of danger.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.780
Amazing, Ri.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:06.990
Ri-san!

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.330
Nice save, Ri-san!

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.920
A direct would definitely have gone in.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.070
Don't worry about it, Tsuguhide.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.130
We've got a corner.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:17.900
Yeah.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.000
That number 14

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.180
should have been on the other 
side of the half line.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.970
So how did he get back here so fast?

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.430
Ri-san, nice save.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.270
Nice cover yourself.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.800
<i>We've been saved by Aizawa's instincts.</i>

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.980
<i>Using his unique prediction ability,</i>

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.890
<i>he determined where the 
opponent would shoot from</i>

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:44.990
<i>and returned in a straight 
line to that point.</i>

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.570
Enoshima's not out 
of the deep end yet.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.820
The Sagamigaura eleven 
are all aiming for

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.740
the goal on this corner kick.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.450
<i>Total Foot isn't just 
an all-man offense.</i>

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.350
<i>The point is to use not just the sides,</i>

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:08.190
<i>but the entire field.</i>

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:10.870
<i>Doing so produces new opportunities and</i>

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.410
<i>chances from situations 
where the opponent</i>

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.350
<i>is unprepared.</i>

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.790
<i>Kazuhide, if you were going to catch</i>

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.380
<i>your opponent off guard 
on a corner kick,</i>

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.590
<i>where would you aim?</i>

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.940
<i>A short corner?</i>

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.360
The corner kick is up high.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.080
It's over the goal and 
towards the opposite side.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.020
<i>All right, nice one, Kazuhide.</i>

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.040
<i>It's an easy shot.</i>

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.810
Tsuguhide Tendo is 
there to receive it.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:42.920
<i>A direct shot!</i>

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.630
It's back to the center!

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.360
This pass goes to number 2, Sega.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.090
<i>It's mine!</i>

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.800
He shoots.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.020
Aizawa gets a piece of it.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.190
The ball isn't stopping yet.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.080
He stops it.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.520
The defensive player,

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.820
Akitoshi Ri, pulls off 
another super save.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.060
<i>It's that number 14 again.</i>

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:15.350
<i>If he hadn't stuck his foot out, 
the ball would definitely</i>

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.870
<i>have gone in.</i>

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.220
Thanks a lot, Ri-san.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.130
I almost scored on our own goal.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.780
Don't be stupid.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.510
If you hadn't put your foot out,

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:27.840
they would have scored.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.500
<i>That's exactly right.</i>

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.360
<i>We've been saved by 
Aizawa's instincts again.</i>

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:36.650
<i>Still, to think they'd change
 sides from a corner kick</i>

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:39.560
<i>to throw the defense off 
before centering the ball...</i>

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.150
The frightening thing is that they pulled off

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.070
that series of plays with direct volleys.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:45.650
Yes.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.800
By connecting with short passes

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.100
and boosting ball possession,

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:54.410
by using the accuracy and
 speed of direct passing,

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.820
they are able to control the 
speed of the game at will.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.430
This will be harder to deal 
with than we thought.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.890
<i>It was close, but that's fine.</i>

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.960
<i>We'll just keep playing like 
this and suck Enoshima</i>

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.450
<i>up in our whirlwind.</i>

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.220
<i>It won't be long before our 
opponents' eyes are spinning</i>

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.550
<i>and they're wobbling on their feet.</i>

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.260
<i>That's the essence of 
new Total Football:</i>

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.310
<i>turning a bad situation 
into an advantage.</i>

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.270
<i>The real weapon is yet to come.</i>

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.990
Let's get back up! Forward, forward!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.500
<i>If we let them shoot any more,</i>

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.650
<i>then why are we, 
the defenders, even here?</i>

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:36.320
Damn it!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.480
Kaiouji!

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:40.110
If you just run away from the 
ball hunting, they'll get you.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:41.290
Head straight for them!

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.540
I know, but it's just hard to do.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:51.670
<i>That's strange.</i>

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.990
<i>In a situation where we are</i>

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.480
<i>mostly in possession of the ball,</i>

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:56.630
<i>why would everyone try to get</i>

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:58.360
<i>rid of the ball so quickly?</i>

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.640
<i>Even Oda-san is usually 
more offensive.</i>

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:05.770
<i>There's something to new Total Football</i>

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.230
<i>that we haven't noticed yet.</i>

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.690
Crap! Mako-san!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.820
All right.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.660
<i>If we keep running around like this,</i>

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.490
<i>we'll be spent by the second half.</i>

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.120
<i>But that said...</i>

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.700
<i>I don't plan on just sitting 
around waiting for it to happen!</i>

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:23.770
Move forward!

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.580
Don't leave Hyodo alone!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.330
Enoshima is moving up the defensive

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.550
line as if pushed forward by a wave.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.420
They're attacking!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.910
I'll call it the "big wave" attack.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:37.670
Like tearing a page out 
of the Total Foot book,

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:39.430
it's an all-man attack!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.770
Don't stick together.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.600
Keep side changes in mind.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:45.570
Right now!

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.230
Here's a side change.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.010
As if laughing at Sagamigaura's defenders,

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:53.690
they switch the stage of 
attack to the other side!

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:55.860
Takase!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.970
Sawamura-san.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:58.640
Okay.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.860
Yoin countered Sagamigaura's 
Total Football

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:07.240
by pulling the defenders 
to one side and then

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.780
switching sides quickly.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.000
However...

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:11.620
What's this?

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.230
They're ball hunting on 
this side as well.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.920
How many players are there?

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:19.250
<i>Shonan, who did the same thing,</i>

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.930
<i>wasn't able to counter them.</i>

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:24.390
Sawamura loses the ball.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:28.230
<i>As I thought, this is a different 
Total Foot than from before.</i>

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.400
Tsuguhide!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.270
Then a short pass to Tsuguhide Tendo.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.480
Go!

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.300
A long feed!

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.940
This long pass goes across 
the center line to Kazuhide,

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:43.910
running into the Enoshima 
defensive area.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.320
No way.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.870
Why is he over there?

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.580
Why you!

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.170
An early cross.

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:52.420
The receiver is...

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.080
Tsuguhide, who should have been

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:57.340
on defense up until now!

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.800
What? What's going on?

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.550
They expected a long pass

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.800
and started running towards the goal.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.510
He stops it.

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:12.560
Another super save by the defender, Ri.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.150
I'll stop you!

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.410
Oda clears it.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.580
Sagamigaura is relentless.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.950
It's a repeated attack from 
the new Total Foot.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.660
<i>Wasn't this guy a defender?</i>

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.410
Crap, crap, crap, crap!

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:30.320
Due to the fast change over,

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.380
other than the defenders, 
Enoshima still isn't back!

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.840
A header contest in front of the goal,

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.300
and the receiver is...

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:41.220
Tsuguhide!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.560
Unbelievable! Ri hits 
it with a side dive!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.520
What?!

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.350
But the ball continues 
towards the post.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.040
Will it be a goal?

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.570
Will it go out?

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.760
Goal!

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.220
Damn it!

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:29.640
The attackers attacked and 
the defenders defended,

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.250
but in the end the goddess 
of victory smiles on

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.600
Sagamigaura and lets the 
ball past the goal post.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.970
0-1, 20 minutes into the first half.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:39.320
<b><i>Enoshima</i></b>

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:39.320
<b><i>Sagamigaura</i></b>

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:39.320
Sagamigaura scores the first goal.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.300
We did it, Kazuhide.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.030
They gave us a tough time, Tsuguhide.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:47.240
Yeah. But we've torn 
open the goal's mouth.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.260
Don't ease up yet!

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.800
Enoshima went to a PK match with Yoin.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.960
I won't allow a single goal!

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.990
Leave it to us!

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:00.830
We're not done yet.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.210
Tsuguhide, you're sounding 
like the coach.

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:06.260
<i>That's right.</i>

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.640
<i>You guys are more than this.</i>

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.500
<i>You've overcome obstacles 
that most would</i>

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.880
<i>give up at.</i>

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:17.750
<i>It's a great thing that 
you've made it this far.</i>

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:25.650
<i>There's no way anyone can 
play soccer on concrete.</i>

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.810
<i>But they kept on playing 
the soccer they could play</i>

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:34.300
<i>in a place like that.</i>

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:40.040
<i>They kept training, and almost all 
of them developed the ability</i>

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.510
<i>to shoot and pass with just one touch.</i>

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:57.560
<i>Most importantly of all, these guys 
love soccer more than anyone.</i>

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.370
<b>New Total Football</b>

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.180
New Total Football.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:15.620
That's right, Kazuhide.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.010
We'll make use of your strengths.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:21.330
You guys are going to 
change high school soccer

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.460
with our new Total Foot.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.540
<b><i>Enoshima</i></b>

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.540
<b><i>Sagamigaura</i></b>

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.090
<i>To change high school soccer.</i>

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.630
<i>Coach's words weren't lies.</i>

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.940
<i>We might be able to do it now.</i>

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.360
Okay.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.190
Over here.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:46.650
Kakeru!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.530
This time!

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.250
This is no good.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:56.160
They've been caught in an 
offsides trap right away.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.930
Again?

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.370
What sort of high 
defensive line is this?

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:01.830
Let's go!

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:06.250
They've gone straight into an 
attack from a fast restart.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.520
<i>We're going to reach higher ground</i>

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.430
<i>and change everything!</i>

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.260
<i>All with our new Total Foot.</i>

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:16.260
Number 10, Kazuhide,

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.230
goes for a long shot without trapping.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.310
It's over goalkeeper Ri's head

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.730
and heading for the goal.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.440
He touches it with his fingertips.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.530
The ball hasn't gone out yet.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.240
Crap, crap, crap, crap!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.430
Horikawa sends it to the 
sides with a sliding kick.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.950
Splendid defense!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.450
There's the whistle.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.910
End of the first half.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:43.300
All right! Great work.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.270
Of course, Coach.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.960
We'll keep it up in the 
second half, as well.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.770
Don't worry!

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:50.170
It's just the first half.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:56.140
0-1. Enoshima goes into 
halftime one goal behind.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:16:01.320
Enoshima didn't really 
get any opportunities.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:02.760
No matter how hard a forward

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:04.270
works in front of his own goal,

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.690
he won't score any points.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.530
Kakerucchi.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.150
Kakeru.

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.020
Really now.

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:31.740
There's still half the game left,

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:34.180
so what are you all looking so gloomy for?

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:37.430
Coach, I know you saw it, too.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.520
We didn't stand a chance 
against Sagamigaura.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:49.410
The score is 0-1, but only because 
of Ri's constant fine saves.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:51.220
I'm sorry, Ri-san.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.610
If we had defended better...

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.450
Oda, Kaiouji, that's not right.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:57.640
Ri-san?

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.650
The distance between 
posts is 7.32 meters.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:04.360
The height of the cross 
bar is 2.44 meters.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.920
Compared to the size of the
 huge field that you defend,

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.570
it's only a small goal mouth.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:12.880
I always play with the intent

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:16.330
to stop any ball that tries 
to go through there.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:19.750
That's why the goal 
that I couldn't stop with

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:23.100
my fingertips was my mistake.

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.470
<i>I thought it was amazing</i>

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.520
<i>that he was able to jump and 
even touch the ball in that situation,</i>

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.820
<i>but he doesn't see it
 as anyone else's fault.</i>

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.600
I won't allow a single goal 
in the second half.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.540
I'll defend that goal.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.190
So catch them.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:38.780
Surpass them somehow, everyone.

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:40.530
Yes, of course.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.580
<i>I was naive.</i>

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.270
<i>There's no way I could take back</i>

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.750
<i>the regular position from this guy</i>

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.750
<i>with just a little effort.</i>

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:51.400
If we lose without Araki,

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:54.300
he'll treat us like idiots 
and say he told us so.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.880
I couldn't stand that.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.010
<i>That's right.</i>

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.100
<i>I would never say that 
we lost because of Araki.</i>

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:06.210
<i>He said that the PK at the 
summer tournament was his fault</i>

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.370
<i>and cried tears of frustration.</i>

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:11.820
<i>If we lose here without him...</i>

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:16.530
<i>Araki, I won't let you say 
it's your fault again.</i>

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.240
<i>We can't lose.</i>

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:22.490
<i>Especially now that Araki-san isn't here.</i>

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.820
<i>We definitely can't lose.</i>

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.030
Oh, that's right.

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:29.290
We have some news about Araki-kun.

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:35.500
At the U-16 Asian 
Tournament's preliminary,

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:39.090
the Japanese representatives 
defeated Thailand, 6-0.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.370
Araki-kun played to his full 
potential as an offensive midfielder

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.240
and claimed three goals,

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.060
the most goals and a hat trick.

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:50.520
Araki.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:51.730
Araki.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.190
Araki-san, amazing.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:58.200
It's time for the second half.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:18:59.910
All right. Let's go!

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.200
Yeah!

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.530
After all that time 
they chased the ball,

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.500
they look so composed.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.330
There must be something.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:20.260
Yes. It doesn't look like we'll be able

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.040
to depend on them tiring out.

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.750
According to the records, aside 
from the sweeper, Rindo-san,

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:28.350
all the defenders have moved 
into the Enoshima penalty area

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.020
and the forwards have been working 
on their half of the field as well.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:32.980
That's strange.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:33.940
Huh?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.430
The score is 0-1, Sagamigaura 
holds a one goal lead

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:39.290
as the second half starts.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.840
Enoshima is playing without 
their ace, Araki,

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.570
but they've still got a fighting chance.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.760
Excuse me, Mishima-san, 
may I see the notes?

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:49.750
Yes.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.060
Comparing the Tendo brothers with

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.920
the movement of the others...

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:01.340
My God. Is this what 
new Total Football is?

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:08.470
I'll stop you.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.110
Wait, Oda-san.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.060
Another player is there 
to receive the pass.

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:16.400
Great teamwork by Sagamigaura.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:22.070
They switch straight 
into an attack by numbers.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.930
Even in the second half,

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.660
their athleticism hasn't faded 
as they hunt for Enoshima's goal!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.490
There's no mistake.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:35.680
New Total Football's all-man
 attack, all-man defense

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:38.170
isn't just supported by athleticism.

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.550
Could it be rotating positions?

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:47.030
Yes. Even if the ideal is an 
all-man attack, all-man defense,

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:49.370
the strategy that the Netherlands 
attempted couldn't be

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.890
accomplished by a high 
school team so easily.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:56.310
When five players attack with

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:59.600
Kazuhide Tendo-kun at the center, 
the remaining four players,

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.710
including Tsuguhide Tendo, 
rest without drawing attention

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:07.070
and slowly move back towards defense.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:11.410
When their attack is stopped

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.750
and the opponent takes 
control of the ball,

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:18.890
the four players who had 
already returned to defense

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:21.020
immediately go to stop the ball

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:22.920
and mark the opponent's attackers.

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:26.140
But the important player here is

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:30.640
the third key man, the 
sweeper, Yuki Rindo-kun.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.850
Only he has never left his side.

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:38.210
He used to play as a 
defender for a youth team.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:41.390
He wasn't a registered player 
during the inter-high.

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:45.110
If you attempt Total Foot 
by interchanging positions,

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:47.870
defense, rather than offense, 
becomes the limiting factor.

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:50.280
During the Yoin match at the inter-high,

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:54.760
it came to light that the defense 
wasn't properly prepared

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:56.830
and they easily lost three goals.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.580
So in order to fill that hole,

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.600
they brought in a
 defense-specific player.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:02.800
Is that right?

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:06.760
Yes. This might be our 
chance to counter.

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:12.180
Tsuguhide-san is already moving forward.

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:15.270
Kazuhide-san is slowly dropping back.

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:17.230
But as he retreats,

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:22.570
he plays a role in the direct plays.

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:26.350
As long as he does this, 
even as he returns to defend,

00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:28.890
it appears as though he 
is part of the attack.

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:31.370
That's why we didn't notice 
the position rotation.

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:34.110
The other thing I noticed from your notes

00:22:34.110 --> 00:22:36.710
was the law of leftward rotation.

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:40.000
He stops it!

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.590
Akitoshi Ri!
 Today, he's a defensive god!

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:46.090
He lays himself on the line

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:48.550
to stop the continuous 
barrage of Sagamigaura shots

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:50.380
like the artillery of a naval fleet.

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:53.040
He's like a god!

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:54.390
Keep them coming!

00:22:54.740 --> 00:22:56.300
Amazing, Ri-san.

00:22:56.770 --> 00:22:58.100
Look carefully.

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:03.930
When he lets go of the 
ball and is free,

00:23:03.930 --> 00:23:06.110
he usually heads to the left.

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:07.940
My notes also indicate, for some reason,

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.070
everyone moves from defense-to-offense,

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:13.340
offense-to-defense in 
a leftward rotation.

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:18.080
Humans tend to prefer 
turning left naturally.

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:21.770
There are a number of theories,

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:25.480
but athletic tracks and merry-go-rounds

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:27.800
are made with the same idea in mind.

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:31.830
Sagamigaura must be 
attempting to reduce

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:38.020
the strain and stress of 
Total Foot by rotating left.

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:39.390
On the other hand,

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:42.680
the Enoshima defenders,
 who have to rotate right,

00:23:42.680 --> 00:23:44.980
experience greater stress than usual.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.370
If that's true,

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:50.170
then coming up with a 
strategy will be difficult.

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:53.200
What can we do against 
nature and psychological tricks?

00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:56.030
If we don't come up with something,

00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:57.540
I don't know how long Ri-san will last.

00:23:57.920 --> 00:23:59.830
True, they're a difficult opponent.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:01.360
But now that we know

00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:03.220
they're employing a leftward rotation,

00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:05.000
we can counter.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.800
Kota-kun, you're up.

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:07.500
Me?

00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:10.290
You'll be the messenger for the strategy

00:24:10.290 --> 00:24:12.090
and go in at the next ball out.

00:24:12.090 --> 00:24:12.930
Okay.

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:15.260
But how will you...

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.150
Their way of fighting is like

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:20.650
what was said to be the 
original draft for Total Foot

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:23.320
which made use of spiral theory,

00:24:23.320 --> 00:24:25.480
the great whirlwind: a Typhoon.

00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:28.440
But there's an eye to a typhoon.

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:30.150
The eye of the typhoon?

00:24:30.810 --> 00:24:34.160
Right. No matter how 
powerful the typhoon,

00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:37.400
there's a windless blue 
sky at the center.

00:24:37.400 --> 00:24:40.000
When that blue sky shines through,

00:24:40.660 --> 00:24:43.630
the knight's spear 
will pierce the goal!

00:24:45.960 --> 00:25:15.360
<b>Next Episode
Kick Off!!</b>

00:24:48.230 --> 00:24:50.910
Sagamigaura 
demonstrates its storm.

00:24:50.910 --> 00:24:53.480
Enoshima finally cracks the 
new Total Football's mystery.

00:24:54.090 --> 00:24:57.220
The bright sunny victory 
that shines through the blue sky

00:24:57.220 --> 00:24:59.300
and the spear of the knight,

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:01.260
Kakeru Aizawa, is now

00:25:01.260 --> 00:25:03.770
piercing the goal of his dreams.

00:25:04.560 --> 00:25:07.540
Next time on Knight in 
the Area, the final episode:

00:25:07.540 --> 00:25:08.690
"Kick Off!!"

00:25:08.690 --> 00:25:09.860
Let's go, Kakeru!

00:25:09.860 --> 00:25:11.470
Yes, Brother!
